"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{B}{B}","name":"Vampire Hexmage","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","oracle_text":"First strike\nSacrifice this creature: Remove all counters from target permanent.","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-08-07","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Vampire Shaman"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If a creature (such as Clone) enters the battlefield as a copy of this creature, the copy’s “enters-the-battlefield” ability will still trigger as long as you cast that creature spell from your hand.","oracle_id":"7dcb95a9-c114-4333-8b45-4380f92d9695","published_at":"2013-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card in a graveyard has {X} in its mana cost, X is 0.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If any abilities trigger on the creature entering the battlefield, those abilities resolve after you lose life. If losing life results in you losing the game, those abilities won't resolve.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, the creature you control from Reanimate is exiled.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The amount of life you lose is determined by the mana value of the card in your graveyard, not the creature once it's on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You lose life after the creature is already on the battlefield. Any abilities it has that interact with loss of life, such as that of Platinum Emperion, apply to that loss of life.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Becoming an artifact doesn't change what color(s) a permanent is.","oracle_id":"f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may target any permanent with the ability, including an artifact.","oracle_id":"f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any permanent can be targeted by the second ability, not just one with counters on it.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Vampire Hexmage's ability can't target a permanent card in a zone other than the battlefield, such as a suspended card.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
